Subject: [PATCH] tuxedo_compatibility_check: allow GIGABYTE DMI vendor

GIGABYTE gaming laptops (G6 KF and relatives) are rebranded Clevo
barebones. They expose the Clevo WMI interface GUIDs
(ABBC0F6B/6C/6D-8EA1-11D1-00A0-C90629100000), so the clevo_wmi /
clevo_acpi / tuxedo_keyboard drivers are the correct drivers for the
keyboard backlight.

However tuxedo_is_compatible() only accepts DMI vendor "TUXEDO", or a CPU
on the legacy skip-list (nothing newer than roughly Intel 12th gen). A
GIGABYTE DMI vendor with a modern CPU fails both checks, so
tuxedo_keyboard aborts with -ENODEV and the RGB keyboard stays dark.

Add GIGABYTE to the DMI allow-list. This is an explicit per-vendor opt-in
rather than a blanket bypass of the compatibility check.

Tested on: GIGABYTE G6 KF (2024), SKU RC56KF, BIOS FD10,
Intel Core i7-13620H, Ubuntu 26.04, tuxedo-drivers 4.24.0.

Signed-off-by: devansh0703 <devansh0703@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c b/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
index ec6fd1a..d3f014b 100644
--- a/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
+++ b/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
@@ -216,6 +216,21 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id tuxedo_dmi_string_match[] = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_CHASSIS_VENDOR, "TUXEDO"),
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "GIGABYTE"),
+		},
+	},
+	{
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "GIGABYTE"),
+		},
+	},
+	{
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_CHASSIS_VENDOR, "GIGABYTE"),
+		},
+	},
 	{ }
 };
 
